# Compiled catalogs are build output: produced by `pnpm i18n:compile` and
# shipped by bin/release/package.sh, never committed. The .po files beside them
# are the source of record and ARE committed.
#
# bin/release/verify-package.sh refuses an archive containing a .po without its
# .mo, which is the check that catches a release that skipped compilation —
# a failure that is otherwise invisible, because the site just renders English.
*.mo
*.json
